===========================================================================
$NetBSD$

Before running the native ispell images, invoke the packaged setup procedure
directly from the DCL process that will use them:

    $ @device:[pkg-prefix.startup]ISPELL_SETUP.COM

Replace "device:[pkg-prefix]" with the native OpenVMS spelling of ${PREFIX}.
The procedure defines DECC$STREAM_PIPE and DECC$POPEN_NO_CRLF_REC_ATTR in the
process logical-name table before image activation.  It also defines the
global DCL foreign-command symbols ISPELL, DEFMT_C, and DEFMT_SH.

You may invoke the procedure from LOGIN.COM.  Do not run it with SPAWN,
because process logical names and command symbols do not propagate from a
subprocess back to its parent.
===========================================================================
